# Kept out of the build context. The Containerfiles COPY only image/,
# features/, installer/ and keys/cosign.pub; the Secure Boot key material
# enters via `podman build --secret`, never via the context.
#
# home/ and dotfiles.sh are listed first on purpose: the dotfiles are NOT part
# of any image and must never become part of one. Excluding them here means a
# stray COPY cannot even reach them.
home
dotfiles.sh

.git
.gitignore
.containerignore
output
docs
.github
**/*.md
Justfile
renovate.json
# the dev container and the VS Code Flatpak, built from their own directory
devtools
# podman reads a -f file directly, so the build does not need it in the
# context; in it, installer/live.Containerfile would land in its own
# `COPY installer/`, and editing a comment would rerun the live build
installer/*.Containerfile

# keys/ stays out of the build context as a whole: the private keys live
# outside the checkout (Justfile, keys_dir), but a copy left in keys/
# (git-ignored *.key) must not reach a build either. The one exception is the
# cosign PUBLIC key: the image needs it to verify its own updates
# (/etc/containers/policy.json), and it is public by definition. Order
# matters, the negation must come after the directory it re-includes from.
keys
!keys/cosign.pub
